Project Alembic usage (project-specific wrappers and examples)

This folder contains Alembic configuration used by the backend service.
The Alembic env.py has been adapted to read the database URL from environment
variables (DATABASE_URL, SQLALCHEMY_DATABASE_URI, DATABASE_URI) and to import
project metadata from `app.shared.models.Base` for autogenerate support


Quick local (PowerShell) examples

# Create an autogenerate revision (inspect the generated file before applying)
python -m alembic -c pwa-marketplace/backend/alembic.ini revision --autogenerate -m "Add Changes"

# Apply all migrations
python -m alembic -c pwa-marketplace/backend/alembic.ini upgrade head

# Generate SQL for a revision without applying (offline SQL)
python -m alembic -c pwa-marketplace/backend/alembic.ini revision --autogenerate -m "msg" --sql


Docker Compose examples (run from repository root)

# Run a revision command inside the backend container (uses sh inside container)
docker compose -f pwa-marketplace/docker-compose.yml exec backend-admin sh -lc 'alembic -c backend/alembic.ini revision --autogenerate -m "autogen"'

# Apply migrations from inside the container
docker compose -f pwa-marketplace/docker-compose.yml exec backend-admin sh -lc 'alembic -c backend/alembic.ini upgrade head'


Notes & troubleshooting

- If autogenerate produces no changes, confirm `app.shared.models` exports `Base` and that
  model definitions reflect your intended schema. If your models file has a different
  name (for example `models_sql2orm.py`), update `backend/alembic/env.py` to import it

- Ensure Alembic runs under the same Python environment that has SQLAlchemy and the
  DB driver (eg: pymysql) installed

- The env.py will accept DATABASE_URL / SQLALCHEMY_DATABASE_URI / DATABASE_URI. When
  running in Docker Compose, prefer setting the env var in the service environment in
  the Compose file or passing it at runtime

- Always review generated migration files before applying them to production


Optional

- Add a Makefile target or small wrapper script that sets the required env var and
  invokes alembic with the project alembic.ini to reduce typing and avoid mistakes
